ass"}, {"turn": 78, "color": "W", "move": "pass", "lead_before": -7.89, "lead_after": -7.94, "points_lost": -0.05, "best": "pass"}, {"turn": 79, "color": "B", "move": "pass", "lead_before": -7.94, "lead_after": -8.0, "points_lost": 0.06, "best": "J8"}], "review": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "title": "The Left-Side Seesaw", "summary": "Opus 5.5 (White) beat the 12k by 8 points after a fight on the left side in which the lead changed hands several times. Both sides had about the same mean loss per move (2.1 against 2.2) and made 6 and 5 blunders respectively. The 12k's A3 (17.8 points) opened a big gap, Opus 5.5's C2 (18.4 points) handed it straight back, and the 12k's D9 then lost 11.3 points to put White ahead for good.", "moments": [{"turn": 12, "text": "Opus 5.5 played B4 here, and Black's lead went from -4.7 to +4.4. That was a 9.1-point loss, and the engine preferred C4. White had been ahead and now trailed."}, {"turn": 15, "text": "The 12k answered with C4, which lost 9.9 points as the lead swung from +5.0 to -4.8. The engine wanted D4. The lead went straight back to White, and Opus 5.5 simply took D4 next at a cost of 0.2."}, {"turn": 21, "text": "The 12k's A3 was the biggest swing of the opening fight. Black's lead went from +0.7 to -17.1, an 17.8-point loss. The engine's choice was G4, away from the corner."}, {"turn": 22, "text": "Opus 5.5 played C2 and gave all of it back. The lead went from -17.1 to +1.2, an 18.4-point loss and the worst move of the game. The engine's choice was H5. The game was level again."}, {"turn": 23, "text": "The 12k played D9 and lost another 11.3 points as the lead went from +1.2 to -10.1. Opus 5.5 was never behind again. The margin settled near 8 points and held through the long endgame to the final W+8."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py parses a pasted board and prints each group's stones and liberties with a danger flag, and count.py counts stones and enclosed territory (with optional dead stones removed) to give a score. Both only inspect the current position as given; neither generates, scores or ranks candidate moves, or plays any continuation.", "stop": false}}